       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. 50 mg of amlodipine daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. You haven't given a clinical reason for it, and I can't think of a scenario in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function where it would be safe. The likely harm is severe, prolonged hypotension and shock, and amlodipine's long half-life means that can last for days.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right now. If more blood pressure control is needed, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide is usually better than going above 10 mg.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's an unusual reason for a supratherapeutic dose, they can review it and enter or co-sign it through the proper channel.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** Make sure 50 mg wasn't carried over from a different drug or a different patient.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
